    <h2 class="section-title">Everything between wanting it and going.</h2>
    <div class="sp-body">
      <p>You want the epic Christmas market weekend with your kid. You have the time and the money and you want to make new memories. What you do not want is everything between wanting it and going.</p>
      <p>Finding out where to go takes too much time. Finding out where to go is overwhelming, and you do not like it. You do not know where to start looking, and it does not feel worth doing all that research.</p>
      <p>Then the questions stack up. Is it worth spending the money if you do not like it. Is it worth doing with your kid. Will you like it as a solo mom with a kid. Will you be overwhelmed. Do you even have the time.</p>
      <p>Then the hotel. You do not know what city to stay in. You do not want a bad location, or somewhere cheap, or somewhere too expensive that is not worth it. Picking a hotel is hard and time consuming, and finding the perfect one takes forever.</p>
      <p>Then where to eat, with too many options. Then what to do each day. Then planning the activities, booking the activities, and building the itinerary day by day.</p>
      <p>That is 12 steps before you ever leave the house. A Christmas market weekend done wrong can easily cost $1,000. Wrong hotel, wrong weekend, tickets you did not book in time, a tired kid and a day spent wandering in circles.</p>
      <p><strong>Sleigh Solo deletes those 12 steps.</strong> Your only steps left are depart, arrive, execute day one, execute day two, and go home.</p>
